WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.330
(bomb swooshing)

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.860
- [Narrator] After
months of brutal fighting

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.901
in the country's east,

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:06.780
(bomb blasting)

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.300
Ukraine is preparing
for its much anticipated

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.523
counter-offensive against Russia.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.280
- Dear Warriors,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.050
the main battles are coming soon.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.133
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.200
(gun shooting)

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.900
- [Narrator] Since Ukraine's
battle plans are confidential,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.610
little is definitively known

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.380
about the coming counter-offensive

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.070
but military experts agree
the stakes couldn't be higher.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.320
- Everyone's been expecting
it, waiting for it.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.940
We dunno exactly when
it's going to happen.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.070
We dunno exactly where
it's going to happen.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.140
- They've got to look at
this counter-offensive

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.710
the way a pool shark
looks at a pool table.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.470
He's not only trying to sink the ball

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.080
but he's also trying
to set his cue ball up

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.120
for a subsequent shot.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.640
- [Narrator] Here's the
situation on the ground right now

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.433
and what to expect on the battlefield.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.020
Since the war began in February of 2022,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.050
Russia has focused its
offensives almost exclusively

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.980
on the east of Ukraine in what's
known as the Donbas region.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.870
- The offensive hasn't been
particularly successful.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.669
They've lost thousands of troops.

00:01:08.669 --> 00:01:10.163
(bomb chinging)

00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:13.080
(bombs blasting)

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.660
They've been using
brutal tactics, shelling,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.150
destroying whole districts.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.290
- [Narrator] After heavy fighting,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.260
the city of Bakmout is
now under Russian control,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.650
Moscow's first major
conquest since last summer.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:29.370
Russia now occupies 17%
of Ukrainian territory,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.500
a stretch of land mass roughly equivalent

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.292
to the size of Iceland.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.890
(bomb blasting)

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.150
- But the Ukrainians are still there.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.160
So the moment what we have is

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.125
something like a a violent stalemate.

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:42.660
(gun cocking)

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.690
- So far, Ukraine's success,
(grenade blasting)

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.070
and Russia's comparatively

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.370
poor performance on the
battlefield has surprised analysts.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.190
- The Russians expected
Kiev to fall in a few days.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.110
They weren't expecting to fight a war.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.890
They were expecting to be
marching in a victory parade.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.723
- [Narrator] Mark Kimmitt

00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:02.280
is retired US Army Brigadier General,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.210
who served in Bosnia, Kosovo, and Iraq.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.290
- Very early on, it was
clear that the Russian forces

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.780
not only did they not have the tactics,

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.930
their equipment proved
incapable of doing that.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.420
And candidly, the
Ukrainians surprised us all

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.850
with both their tactical ability

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.190
and their equipment as well.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.150
(tanker engine rumbling)
(bomb blasting)

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:29.150
- We will never submit to
any foreigners or colonizers.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.470
That's why we fight

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.910
- [Narrator] From the
beginning of the war,

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.530
Ukrainian President, Zelenskyy,

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.840
made it clear that his aim is to liberate

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.510
all Ukrainian territory including Crimea

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.010
and parts of Eastern Ukraine

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.380
that were first occupied in 2014.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.043
- That seems an unlikely goal
for the immediate defensive

00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:51.277
(bombs clanging)

00:02:51.277 --> 00:02:52.410
(bomb blasting)

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.592
because that's a big ask.

00:02:54.592 --> 00:02:57.120
That's a lot of Russian troops, you know,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.800
who are well dug in.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.890
- We do not have that much artillery but

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.890
we do stay strong because we
do have troops on our side.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.680
- Western weapons have
been trickling into Ukraine

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.330
since the start of the war.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.350
More recently,

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.991
there's been a steady
escalation of deliveries.

00:03:15.991 --> 00:03:18.600
(tanker gun cocking)
(gun shooting)

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.510
- Its own Soviet stocks
have been supplemented

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.200
by large supplies of weapons from the West

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.050
and these are included long-range

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.095
rocket artillery systems called HIMARS.

00:03:31.095 --> 00:03:33.360
(bomb blasting)

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.220
More recently, you've had the West

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.410
has provided battle tanks.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:41.280
- Hopefully they've got
enough armored vehicles

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.500
and enough tanks to make that punch

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.750
necessary for a counter-offensive.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.800
But most important,

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.920
they're going to need the
intelligence from drones,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.720
perhaps from satellites,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.640
to get a good idea of the weakest
point of the Russian front

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.460
because naturally that's
where they want to attack

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.110
- [Narrator] Ahead of
its counter-offensive,

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.860
Ukraine has been carrying
out drone attacks.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.690
The aim is to weaken the Russians

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.540
ahead of the broader ground campaign.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.210
The current frontline stretches 900 miles

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.790
from the south of Ukraine
all the way around

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.830
the east up to the Northeast.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.600
That's roughly the equivalent distance

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.240
between New Orleans and Chicago.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.090
- So I don't think anybody,
at this point, can predict

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.790
the likely attack routes

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.950
but they certainly can predict

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.370
a number of attack routes
that they would use.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.340
- [Narrator] General Kimmitt
envisions four likely scenarios

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.500
that the Ukrainian forces might attempt

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.720
to kick off their counter-offensive.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.530
- Well, I think the
first avenue of approach

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.510
I think the most obvious counter attack

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:50.510
would be from Kherson over
towards the sea of Sea of Azov.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.300
It would have a significant tactical value

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.060
because it would cut this land bridge

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.980
that is so vital to the Russians

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.670
between Crimea and to the
rear of the Russian forces,

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:06.384
not only for logistics purposes

00:05:06.384 --> 00:05:08.760
but to demonstrate to the world

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.060
that the Russians own all that area

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:15.240
between Crimea and Luhansk.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.730
The second likely attack routes would be

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.880
from Zaporizhzhia down to Berdyansk.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.690
It has very good roads that
make a counter offensive

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.010
easier to operate with wheeled

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.730
and track vehicles which
will be critical to this war.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.800
I think the third attack route

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.370
would be through Donetsk down to Mariupol.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.800
It wouldn't have the tactical value

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.140
as much of cutting that land bridge

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.110
because the land bridge would remain open

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:50.040
between Crimea and a significant amount

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.800
of the Russian forces.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.800
But the strategic communications
value of retaking Mariupol,

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:02.430
that city where the Ukrainians encountered

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.710
probably their biggest defeat,

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.592
I don't think you can overstate the value

00:06:06.592 --> 00:06:11.580
of retaking Mariupol and
getting into the Russian minds

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.043
that they have encountered
a significant defeat.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:19.260
The last option, I think that
the Ukrainians would have

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.350
would be attacking due east from Kharkiv

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.230
to right in through Luhansk.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:29.040
That would have a
significant strategic effect

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.550
because you now would be
on the borders of Russia

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.250
and that would be sending a clear message

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.870
to the Russian people

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.630
that the Ukrainians are able to take back

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:43.110
much of the land that they lost in 2014.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.610
- [Narrator] Despite the Ukrainian's

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.553
impressive battlefield record thus far,

00:06:46.553 --> 00:06:50.195
Kimmitt is cautious about
making optimistic predictions.

00:06:50.195 --> 00:06:51.990
(gun shooting)

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.450
- I don't believe that the Ukrainians

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:58.980
will be able to achieve a complete routing

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.480
of the Russians such
that they would withdraw

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.380
from both Crimea and the Ukraine.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.030
And candidly, I don't think,

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.690
unless there's an absolute
collapse of the Russian forces,

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.625
that that will happen in the next year.

00:07:14.625 --> 00:07:15.540
(taker rumbling)

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.230
My major milestone is how deep do they get

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.390
into Ukrainian territory.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:25.979
I'd like to see them
get as far as the water.

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:27.090
(gun shooting)

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.870
They've got to decisively
defeat the Russians

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.000
for this to be a
successful counter attack.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.120
And it's got to be successful enough

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.690
that it will continue to inspire the West

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.520
to provide material and equipment

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.250
for the next counter attack

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.170
and the next counter attack after that

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.810
because this certainly
will not end the war.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.550
- Ukrainian officials have also

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.910
been quite keen to play down the sort of,

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.560
the larger aims of the offensive.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.720
They recognize that it's not the case

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.100
that they'll suddenly be able to take back

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.410
all of Ukrainian Ty just
from this offensive.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.950
They see this as one offensive,
the next phase in the war.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.210
It's an important offensive,

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.800
it's a critical offensive,

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.123
but it's not the be all and all.

00:08:10.123 --> 00:08:13.373
(soft twinkling music)

